Rob Ellwood wrote on 07/06/2003 10:42 PM:
> Stanislav Traykov wrote:
>> 
>>   [Directly looting containers inside other containers.]
> 
> 	I suggest that you make nested looting take one turn.
> 
> 	(As a side benefit, this eliminates concerns of players
> becoming overtaxed part way through the unpack / repack actions.)

This (along with the appendix) sounds reasonable to me. Perhaps it
should take two turns, or 1/2 per nesting level.. But one really should
be able to open a container _within_ another one (thus not getting
encumbered from things one doesn't really remove from a BoH) -- it's
logical.

However one major change this would bring is what Roger Broadbent noted:
BoHs will be immune to cursing when contained even when used. Currenly,
nesting the BoH is a tradeoff between time cost+being bored and security
over said BoH's buc status. If there's a consensus that the time to loot
nested containers could be decreased then only being bored is not to be
considered a game-balancing issue, IMO.

The other major change, magical explosions, is easy to account for. The
code just checks on each step whether the applied container can be
inserted in the outer one without problems and a magical explosion is
produced if not so. However it would be illogical to have explosions if
we are not really removing containers from containers!(?)

As it is we have two important elements of the game that would be changed:

1. getting one's bag cursed
2. looting nested BoH's

I think #1 is not unbalancing. If one opts for keeping the BoH in a
sack, the chance that it will get cursed on the two turns it's out is
minimal. (And two turns is exaggerated time for that operation.)

It's an option many players don't make because it is boring with the
current interface, not because it's bad strategy. If convinient means of
accessing the inner BoH is provided this would be the way to go and BoH
just won't get cursed--because the game got a better interface, not
because it was made easier.

#2 is IMO the one that needs consideration. If there's nothing to
prevent players from using already nested BoHs without risk it really
makes things different.

For this issue we need a YANI that would provide balance. It would be
easiest to calculate the same chance as above (which is the same as the
step-by-step version would have) and cause magical explosions when
applying. The BoHs just don't like it being inside another one and
explode (with the appropriate probability) even when only fiddled with?
The outer one catches the explosion and goes boom as a "bonus"?

As said, I'm very interested on YANIs about this. I need to decide
whether that patch will just mimick the classic behaviour and be a
convenience patch or perhaps, as Rob Ellwood encouraged me to think,
there's room for a more major change?

greetings,
